I take my bill from the table.
I go to the front counter.
The elderly man is sitting there.
I give that paper slip to him.
"Uncle, this is my bill," I say.
"One hundred and fifty rupees, madam," he says.
I take out exactly one hundred and fifty rupees from my purse.
"Here is the money," I say.
He takes the money.
"Uncle, can I get a receipt for this?" I ask.
"Yes madam, you will definitely get it," he says.
He gives me the receipt.
"Uncle, the tea and bun maska here was very nice," I say.
"I also liked the mawa cake a lot," I tell him.
"Thank you madam, definitely come again," he says with a smile.
"Yes, thank you very much," I say.
I step out of the café.
It is evening now.
The street outside is very bustling.
